{"url": "https://x.com/weeb3dev/status/2101063917959311821", "id": "2101063917959311821", "text": "Obsidian, as a @Grok @Bot.\n\nI encountered a real pain point while working with one of my teams of Grok Bots. I couldn't view nor edit Markdown files directly inside our shared agent computer. \n\nNo real editor, no graph, no second brain. So Dr Eggbot (by @poteto) and I co-designed the Grok Bot obsidian: a CLI-first @obsdmd specialist that owns a local vault on the Grok computer. \n\nIt installs/configures Obsidian, seeds a vault, and creates \u00b7 edits \u00b7 links \u00b7 searches notes with Obsidian Flavored Markdown. Prefers obsidian CLI over GUI clicking. Optional Web Clipper for capture-from-Chrome into the vault. Extend functionality with plugins. \n\nOther bots can write durable notes into it, too. It plugs into whatever workflow you already run. I now use Obsidian with my Job Hunt crew of Grok Bots. \n\nTemplate: https://x.ai/bot/tukhb8f4XyUJFkRWlHWaz", "raw_text": {"text": "Obsidian, as a @Grok @Bot.\n\nI encountered a real pain point while working with one of my teams of Grok Bots. I couldn't view nor edit Markdown files directly inside our shared agent computer. \n\nNo real editor, no graph, no second brain. So Dr Eggbot (by @poteto) and I co-designed the Grok Bot obsidian: a CLI-first @obsdmd specialist that owns a local vault on the Grok computer. \n\nIt installs/configures Obsidian, seeds a vault, and creates \u00b7 edits \u00b7 links \u00b7 searches notes with Obsidian Flavored Markdown. Prefers obsidian CLI over GUI clicking. Optional Web Clipper for capture-from-Chrome into the vault. Extend functionality with plugins. \n\nOther bots can write durable notes into it, too. It plugs into whatever workflow you already run. I now use Obsidian with my Job Hunt crew of Grok Bots. \n\nTemplate: https://t.co/0G9zrcd1Ry", "display_text_range": [0, 835], "facets": [{"type": "mention", "indices": [15, 20], "original": "Grok", "id": "1720665183188922368"}, {"ty